# AVI ELF II / Hyperboard 32 KiB ROM — Netronics-compatible experiment.
# Approved architecture: docs/AVI_NETRONICS_ROM_APPROVED_DESIGN.md
# Reversible development only. Do not overwrite the proven 875B One ROM.
#
# CPU logical ROM address   Allocated     Component
# $8000-$97FF               6144 bytes    AVI / Elf2K monitor
# $9800-$A0FF               2304 bytes    AVI HELP
# $A100-$A3FF                768 bytes    reserved
# $A400-$B0FF               3328 bytes    EDTASM (XMODEM S/L disabled)
# $B100-$C1FF               4352 bytes    reserved
# $C200-$EFFF              11776 bytes    reserved for future services
# $F000-$F0FF                256 bytes    ORIGINAL GIANT MONITOR, unchanged
# $F100-$F2FF                512 bytes    reserved
# $F300-$FFFF               3328 bytes    extended BIOS/BIOS
#
# COM1 bit-banged Q/EF4 default, nominal 2400. Requires EF4 hardware jumper.
# COM2 CDP1854 is optional: 9600 8N1 presently proven.
# COM2 19200/38400 deliberately REJECTED pending clock/hardware validation.
# Netronics Tiny BASIC executes separately from RAM starting at $0000.
#
# This configuration affects ONLY the AVI variant; stock Elf2K builds intact.
BOOTS=08000H
WARMB=($(strip $(BOOTS))+3)
RAMPAGE=07F00H

HELP=09800H
BIOS=0FF00H
EBIOS=0F800H
EDTASM=0A400H
GIANT=0F000H
